-- wp32_billing (WP-32; billing-12, 14, 15, 19, 37, 38, 39; database-75, 76, 79, 82; _db/billing.md M1, M2). Expand-only: the
-- previous release runs unchanged on this file. Its inserts name neither status nor processed_at, so the defaults below are
-- its row shape (`processed`, no outcome), and the consistency check lets outcome stay null until WP-46 tightens it.
--
-- Generated by drizzle-kit generate, then these hand edits, all below the generated part:
--   1. stripe_events.received_at backfilled from processed_at, so retention counts from the real day.
--   2. credit_balances: storage parameters, then the backfill under a SHARE lock with its triggers in one transaction, so no
--      ledger or application write is missed or counted twice. The SHARE lock stops writers for that moment and the runner
--      retries on lock_timeout. Ledger first: settlement writes the ledger before applications, so this order cannot wait on
--      a writer that waits on it.
--   3. ensure_credit_balance, credit_ledger_apply, applications_in_flight and the two triggers (_db/billing.md 5), with one
--      deviation: both triggers upsert except on a DELETE, so no user with a ledger row or an in-flight application can lack
--      a row. A DELETE only updates: in the "user" cascade the balance row may already be gone, and inserting it again would
--      fail its foreign key.
--      ensure_credit_balance makes nothing for a user that does not exist, instead of failing its foreign key: a request whose
--      account was erased while it waited finds no row, and no application either, rather than a 500.
--   4. effective_plan, the SQL mirror of effectivePlan (database-76); the shared vectors are in test/credit-balances.int.test.ts.
--
-- Grants are in ops/provision-roles.sql. EXECUTE is revoked from PUBLIC here because development and test databases have no
-- roles. The trigger functions need no grant: a trigger fires whoever writes the row.

CREATE TABLE "credit_balances" (
	"user_id" text PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
	"balance" integer NOT NULL,
	"in_flight" integer DEFAULT 0 NOT NULL,
	"updated_at" timestamp with time zone DEFAULT now() NOT NULL
);
